<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cai Tingkai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1892">1892</a>–<a href="/years/1968">1968</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cai Tingkai was a Chinese general who commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/19th-route-army">19th Route Army</a> in its defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1932. Sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> to fight the Communists, he and other dissidents broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a> and proclaimed the Fujian People's Government in November 1933, which collapsed within two months. He later held posts in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cai-tingkai.jpg" alt="Cai Tingkai" width="290" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%94%A1%E5%BB%B7%E9%94%B4%E7%AD%BE%E5%90%8D%E7%85%A7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
